  "stem": "The expression \\((4x - 1)(x + 3) - 11x\\) is equivalent to \\(ax^{2} + c\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(c\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(a - c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "7"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Expand: \\((4x - 1)(x + 3) = 4x^{2} + 12x - x - 3 = 4x^{2} + 11x - 3\\).",
    "Subtract \\(11x\\): \\(4x^{2} - 3\\), so \\(a = 4\\) and \\(c = -3\\).",
    "\\(a - c = 4 - (-3) = 7\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\np = Poly(expand((4*x - 1)*(x + 3) - 11*x), x)\nassert p.coeff_monomial(x) == 0\na, c = p.coeff_monomial(x**2), p.coeff_monomial(1)\nassert a - c == 7\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [a - c]",
